  "given": {
    "O": "The centre of a rosette.",
    "A": "Any point to the right of O. OA is the radius of the rosette’s circle."
  },
  "steps": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Rule a horizontal line through O and A and draw a circle about O through A: the circle of one rosette.",
      "create": {"c": {"circle": {"centre": "O", "through": "A"}}, "h": {"line": {"through": ["O", "A"]}}},
      "animate": "compass"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Rule the vertical through O. At the four points where the circle meets the two lines, rule lines at right angles to them: the square cell the rosette sits in. Its sides are where this rosette meets its neighbours.",
      "textWithoutHelpers": "Rule the vertical through O. Where the circle meets the two lines, rule lines at right angles to them on the left, the right and the top: three sides of the square cell the rosette sits in. Its sides are where this rosette meets its neighbours.",
      "create": {
        "v": {"line": {"through": "O", "perpendicularTo": "h"}},
        "P0": {"point": {"meet": ["c", "h"], "pick": {"angle": 0.0}}},
        "P180": {"point": {"meet": ["c", "h"], "pick": {"angle": 180.0}}},
        "P90": {"point": {"meet": ["c", "v"], "pick": {"angle": 90.0}}},
        "P270": {"point": {"meet": ["c", "v"], "pick": {"angle": 270.0}}},
        "gx": {"line": {"through": "P0", "perpendicularTo": "h"}},
        "gxw": {"line": {"through": "P180", "perpendicularTo": "h"}},
        "gy": {"line": {"through": "P90", "perpendicularTo": "v"}},
        "gys": {"line": {"through": "P270", "perpendicularTo": "v"}},
        "K": {"point": {"meet": ["gx", "gy"]}},
        "K2": {"point": {"meet": ["gxw", "gy"]}},
        "K3": {"point": {"meet": ["gxw", "gys"]}},
        "K4": {"point": {"meet": ["gx", "gys"]}},
        "r45": {"line": {"through": ["O", "K"]}}
      },
      "highlight": ["c", "h"],
      "animate": "ruler"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Keep the compass open to the radius. Put its point on each of the four points on the circle and draw a circle through O: they cut the circle at eight more points, so it is divided into twelve.",
      "create": {
        "cE": {"circle": {"centre": "P0", "through": "O"}},
        "cW": {"circle": {"centre": "P180", "through": "O"}},
        "cN": {"circle": {"centre": "P90", "through": "O"}},
        "cS": {"circle": {"centre": "P270", "through": "O"}},
        "P60": {"point": {"meet": ["c", "cE"], "pick": {"angle": 60.0}}},
        "P300": {"point": {"meet": ["c", "cE"], "pick": {"angle": 300.0}}},
        "P120": {"point": {"meet": ["c", "cW"], "pick": {"angle": 120.0}}},
        "P240": {"point": {"meet": ["c", "cW"], "pick": {"angle": 240.0}}},
        "P30": {"point": {"meet": ["c", "cN"], "pick": {"angle": 30.0}}},
        "P150": {"point": {"meet": ["c", "cN"], "pick": {"angle": 150.0}}},
        "P210": {"point": {"meet": ["c", "cS"], "pick": {"angle": 210.0}}},
        "P330": {"point": {"meet": ["c", "cS"], "pick": {"angle": 330.0}}}
      },
      "highlight": ["P0", "P90", "P180", "P270"],
      "animate": "compass"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Join each of the twelve points to the one 60° round: two hexagons. Their twelve sides, carried on as full lines, cross the cell and run into the neighbouring cells.",
      "create": {
        "H0": {"line": {"through": ["P0", "P60"]}},
        "H1": {"line": {"through": ["P30", "P90"]}},
        "H2": {"line": {"through": ["P60", "P120"]}},
        "H3": {"line": {"through": ["P90", "P150"]}},
        "H4": {"line": {"through": ["P120", "P180"]}},
        "H5": {"line": {"through": ["P150", "P210"]}},
        "H6": {"line": {"through": ["P180", "P240"]}},
        "H7": {"line": {"through": ["P210", "P270"]}},
        "H8": {"line": {"through": ["P240", "P300"]}},
        "H9": {"line": {"through": ["P270", "P330"]}},
        "H10": {"line": {"through": ["P300", "P0"]}},
        "H11": {"line": {"through": ["P330", "P30"]}}
      },
      "animate": "ruler"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Rule the lines through O and opposite points, and halve the angles between them: a line through O every 15°.",
      "textWithoutHelpers": "Rule the lines through O and the opposite points at 30°, 60°, 120° and 150°.",
      "create": {
        "r30": {"line": {"through": ["P30", "P210"]}},
        "r60": {"line": {"through": ["P60", "P240"]}},
        "r120": {"line": {"through": ["P120", "P300"]}},
        "r150": {"line": {"through": ["P150", "P330"]}},
        "r15": {"line": {"through": "O", "bisects": ["P0", "O", "P30"]}},
        "r75": {"line": {"through": "O", "bisects": ["P60", "O", "P90"]}},
        "r105": {"line": {"through": "O", "bisects": ["P90", "O", "P120"]}},
        "r165": {"line": {"through": "O", "bisects": ["P150", "O", "P180"]}},
        "r135": {"line": {"through": "O", "perpendicularTo": "r45"}}
      },
      "animate": "ruler"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The hexagon sides cross each other on the 15°, 45°, 75°… lines. Draw the circle about O through one of these crossings; it touches all twelve sides.",
      "create": {
        "X45": {"point": {"meet": ["H0", "H1"]}},
        "co": {"circle": {"centre": "O", "through": "X45"}}
      },
      "animate": "compass"
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "text": "Mark where this circle meets the vertical and the 195° line, and join the two marks. Where the chord crosses the horizontal, draw a circle about O: the inner circle the star is built on.",
      "create": {
        "U90": {"point": {"meet": ["co", "v"], "pick": {"angle": 90.0}}},
        "U195": {"point": {"meet": ["co", "r15"], "pick": {"angle": 195.0}}},
        "chord": {"line": {"through": ["U90", "U195"]}},
        "T": {"point": {"meet": ["chord", "h"]}},
        "ci": {"circle": {"centre": "O", "through": "T"}}
      },
      "animate": "compass"
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "text": "Mark where the inner circle meets the lines at 0°, 30°, 60° and so on, and join each mark to the one 150° round: twelve lines, the twelve-pointed star.",
      "create": {
        "Q0": {"point": {"meet": ["ci", "h"], "pick": {"angle": 0.0}}},
        "Q30": {"point": {"meet": ["ci", "r30"], "pick": {"angle": 30.0}}},
        "Q60": {"point": {"meet": ["ci", "r60"], "pick": {"angle": 60.0}}},
        "Q90": {"point": {"meet": ["ci", "v"], "pick": {"angle": 90.0}}},
        "Q120": {"point": {"meet": ["ci", "r120"], "pick": {"angle": 120.0}}},
        "Q150": {"point": {"meet": ["ci", "r150"], "pick": {"angle": 150.0}}},
        "Q180": {"point": {"meet": ["ci", "h"], "pick": {"angle": 180.0}}},
        "Q210": {"point": {"meet": ["ci", "r30"], "pick": {"angle": 210.0}}},
        "Q240": {"point": {"meet": ["ci", "r60"], "pick": {"angle": 240.0}}},
        "Q270": {"point": {"meet": ["ci", "v"], "pick": {"angle": 270.0}}},
        "Q300": {"point": {"meet": ["ci", "r120"], "pick": {"angle": 300.0}}},
        "Q330": {"point": {"meet": ["ci", "r150"], "pick": {"angle": 330.0}}},
        "A0": {"line": {"through": ["Q0", "Q150"]}},
        "A1": {"line": {"through": ["Q30", "Q180"]}},
        "A2": {"line": {"through": ["Q60", "Q210"]}},
        "A3": {"line": {"through": ["Q90", "Q240"]}},
        "A4": {"line": {"through": ["Q120", "Q270"]}},
        "A5": {"line": {"through": ["Q150", "Q300"]}},
        "A6": {"line": {"through": ["Q180", "Q330"]}},
        "A7": {"line": {"through": ["Q210", "Q0"]}},
        "A8": {"line": {"through": ["Q240", "Q30"]}},
        "A9": {"line": {"through": ["Q270", "Q60"]}},
        "A10": {"line": {"through": ["Q300", "Q90"]}},
        "A11": {"line": {"through": ["Q330", "Q120"]}}
      },
      "animate": "ruler"
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "text": "Four small hexagons sit round each corner of the cell. Where the 60° line from O crosses the top of the cell is the centre of one. Open the compass to where a hexagon side crosses the top of the cell, and draw the circle: it marks the hexagon’s inner corner on the top of the cell. Do the same on the right side of the cell with the 30° line.",
      "create": {
        "Hc": {"point": {"meet": ["r60", "gy"]}},
        "Ho": {"point": {"meet": ["H0", "gy"]}},
        "ch": {"circle": {"centre": "Hc", "through": "Ho"}},
        "Hi": {"point": {"meet": ["ch", "gy"], "pick": {"angle": 53.794}}},
        "Hc2": {"point": {"meet": ["r30", "gx"]}},
        "Ho2": {"point": {"meet": ["H1", "gx"]}},
        "ch2": {"circle": {"centre": "Hc2", "through": "Ho2"}},
        "Hi2": {"point": {"meet": ["ch2", "gx"], "pick": {"angle": 36.206}}}
      },
      "highlight": ["K"],
      "animate": "compass"
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "text": "Through each inner corner, rule the hexagon’s two missing sides and carry them on to the diagonal of the cell: at 60° and 120° through the corner on the top, at 30° and 150° through the corner on the side. Where they meet the diagonal, they close the octagon at the corner.",
      "create": {
        "G1": {"line": {"through": "Hi", "parallelTo": "r60"}},
        "G2": {"line": {"through": "Hi", "parallelTo": "r120"}},
        "G3": {"line": {"through": "Hi2", "parallelTo": "r30"}},
        "G4": {"line": {"through": "Hi2", "parallelTo": "r150"}}
      },
      "animate": "ruler"
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "text": "Copy the corner’s hexagons and octagon to the other three corners of the cell, turning them about O.",
      "create": {"Gr": {"repeat": {"of": ["G1", "G2", "G3", "G4"], "by": "rot4"}}},
      "animate": "ruler"
    },
    {
